      "body": "## Motivation\n\nClaude Code sends `thinking: {\"type\": \"adaptive\"}` on every `/v1/messages` request, including with a local model name. On a server started without `--reasoning-parser` (any instruct-only model), SGLang answers each of those requests with:\n\n```\nHTTP 400 invalid_request_error: Anthropic thinking is not supported for models without a reasoning parser\n```\n\nSo Claude Code can't use an instruct model on SGLang at all: with Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507, 0 of 6 requests got an answer. The same request without `thinking` gets 200.\n\nWith `adaptive`, the model decides whether to think, and Anthropic's docs say \"Thinking is optional for the model\". A model that can't think should answer without a thinking block instead of failing the request.\n\nReproduce (any model, no `--reasoning-parser`):\n\n```\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 --port 30000\ncurl -s localhost:30000/v1/messages -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"model\":\"m\",\"max_tokens\":64,\"thinking\":{\"type\":\"adaptive\"},\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Say hi.\"}]}'\n```\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `entrypoints/anthropic/serving.py`: `adaptive` still maps to reasoning on, except when the chat server has no reasoning parser; then it maps to off. An explicit `{\"type\": \"enabled\"}` keeps its 400, so a client that really asks for thinking still finds out it can't have it.\n- `test_serving.py`: the fake chat server gets a `reasoning_parser`, and a new test checks that `adaptive` without one calls `apply_reasoning_enabled(False)`. It fails on main and passes here.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo change to model outputs. Only requests that used to get a 400 behave differently.\n\nVerified with a real Claude Code 2.1.316 session against Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507:\n- On main e33cd0c3a1: 0 of 6 requests answered.\n- With this fix and #45129 (the `display` fix) applied: 4 of 4 answered, and the coding task finished.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] pre-commit passes.\n- [x] Unit test added (`test_request_thinking_adaptive_without_reasoning_parser_is_disabled`).\n- [ ] Docs: no change needed.\n\nI used Claude Code to trace the bug and draft the fix and test; I reviewed the change and reran the test myself.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41660872064](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41660872064)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41660872486](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41660872486)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41660872050](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41660872050)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
